// Author: Calvin Quint
// GitHub: https://github.com/calvin-quint/docs/blob/main/01-detection-engineering/kql/teams/non_user_actors_amazon_isp.kql
// Non-User Actor in Teams from Amazon ISP
// MITRE ATT&CK: Collection — Automated Collection (T1119)
// Detects: Teams activity where the acting entity's Role is "Actor" but its
//          Type is not "User" (a bot/application identity, not a person),
//          sourced from AWS infrastructure. Narrows the ISP-wide rule down
//          to confirmed non-human actors — the strongest signal that an
//          automated bot (rather than an employee on a cloud VPN) is
//          operating inside a meeting.
CloudAppEvents
| where Application contains "Teams"
| where ISP contains "Amazon"
| extend ParsedObjects = parse_json(ActivityObjects)
| mv-expand obj = ParsedObjects
| extend Role = tostring(obj.Role), Type = tostring(obj.Type)
| where Role == "Actor" and Type != "User"
